window.RULES_REFERENCE_HTML="<span class=\"eyebrow\">MANDATORY HARD RULES \u00b7 V1</span><h2>Every required check has veto power.</h2><p><b>ATC:</b> pairwise radar \u22653 NM; legacy wake matrix heavy\u2192heavy 4 NM, heavy\u2192large 5 NM, heavy\u2192small 6 NM, large\u2192small 4 NM. Close parallel arrival runways share wake constraints below 2,500 ft. Constant follower groundspeed converts slot gaps to NM. Arrivals and runway takeoffs cannot use closed runways; onward takeoff time includes the configured taxi-out after gate departure. Every taxi segment must be unblocked.</p><p><b>Pilot:</b> holding must preserve destination fuel, required alternate fuel and the larger of entered reserve or 45 minutes normal cruise burn. Severe/intense storm routes require assessed clearance \u226520 miles; arrivals cannot use weather-closed windows. Diversions require an available, coordinate-defined alternate, enough time to reach it and fuel including final reserve.</p><p><b>Ground:</b> gate occupancy lasts until planned departure, followed by the configured buffer (default 10 min). Turnaround must meet the configured minimum (default 40 min). Onward flight completion must fit the supplied remaining FDP budget, and remaining flying must fit the daily flight-time budget. Ground-team capacity is separate from flight-crew duty.</p><p>Required unknown data gives <b>NOT EVALUATED</b> and blocks both consensus and fallback. For a diversion, destination ground checks are explicitly not applicable. Connection transfer (default 45 min), overtime and turnaround delay are preferences after all hard checks.</p><p><b>Scope:</b> executable hackathon rules, not certification or a complete FAA/Part 117 implementation. Crew budgets and weather assessments are synthetic scenario inputs.</p><p><a href=\"rules.json\" target=\"_blank\">Download rule configuration</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"scenario-example.json\" target=\"_blank\">Example scenario</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/Order/7110.65BB_Basic_dtd_2-20-25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FAA wake standard</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-14/chapter-I/subchapter-G/part-121/subpart-U/section-121.639\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Domestic fuel requirements</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/aim/aim0701.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FAA weather guidance</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-14/chapter-I/subchapter-G/part-117/section-117.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flight duty period</a></p>";